<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>61.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <name>Has_Quote</name>
        <label>Has An Existing Quote?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>242</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Quote Yet - Skip</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Quote_Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Existing_Quote.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Existing_Deduction_Line</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Quote Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Line_Already_Exists</name>
        <label>Deduction Line Already Exists?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>458</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_TradeIn_Product</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Add It</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Already_Exists</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Existing_Deduction_Line.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <label>Already Exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Real gap found 2026-09-08 re-checking BRD AC2 literally: &quot;Given a trade-in value is approved, When the Sales Representative opens the quotation, Then the trade-in value appears as a negative line item&quot; — AF_FL_Opp_CreateQuotation only adds the Trade-In Deduction line if an Approved Appraisal already exists AT THE MOMENT the Quote is created. Since Quote creation and trade-in evaluation/approval can easily happen in either order in real use (a rep can create the Quote while the Used Car Team is still evaluating), a Trade-In approved AFTER its Opportunity&apos;s Quote already exists never got the deduction line — AC2 was only true for one specific sequencing, not &quot;whenever approved&quot;. This flow closes that: finds the Opportunity via ReferenceRecordId, finds its existing Quote(s), and adds the same Trade-In Deduction line (same Product2/PricebookEntry as AF_FL_Opp_CreateQuotation uses) to any Quote that doesn&apos;t already have one for this specific Appraisal — safe to run even if AF_FL_Opp_CreateQuotation already added it (the AF_RelatedTradeIn__c-based existence check prevents a duplicate either way). SECOND real gap found live 2026-09-08 during a full-persona-cycle test: originally fired on AF_ApprovalStatus__c reaching Approved alone, but a validation rule (AF_VR_QLI_TradeInDeductionGate, LFRDN-630 - pre-existing in the org, not authored this session) requires the linked Trade-In to ALSO have AF_TradeInOutcome__c = &quot;Accepted&quot; before a Trade-In Deduction line can be created; Approved alone throws FIELD_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_EXCEPTION and blocks the Appraisal save entirely. AF_TradeInOutcome__c is described in its own field metadata as &quot;Rep-recorded outcome&quot; - a second, later step the initiating rep performs after Used Car Team approval (matches AF_FL_Appraisal_ApprovalApproved&apos;s own notification text: &quot;Record the customer outcome and continue with the quotation&quot;). Retargeted the trigger to fire on AF_TradeInOutcome__c reaching Accepted instead of AF_ApprovalStatus__c reaching Approved - this is the actually-correct BRD-consistent moment, and satisfies the validation rule&apos;s real precondition. NOTE: AF_FL_Opp_CreateQuotation (the original RS-06 flow, out of this session&apos;s scope) has the SAME latent gap - it also never checks AF_TradeInOutcome__c before creating its own inline deduction line, so a Quote created for an Opportunity whose Appraisal is Approved but not yet Accepted will also fail this validation rule. Flagged for the user, not fixed here (RS-06 is a different story). THIRD real gap found live in QA: Product2Id/PricebookEntryId for the Trade-In Deduction line were hardcoded to DEV-specific record Ids, which do not exist in QA (or any other org) - Ids are never portable across orgs. Fixed by looking up Product2 by ProductCode=&apos;AF-TRADEIN-DEDUCT&apos; and its active PricebookEntry on the Quote&apos;s own Pricebook2Id (Get_TradeIn_Product / Get_TradeIn_PricebookEntry), instead of hardcoded literals - this is org-portable and also correctly respects a Quote on a non-Standard Pricebook, which the old hardcoded PricebookEntryId could never do.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_NegativeTradeInValue</name>
        <dataType>Currency</dataType>
        <expression>0 - {!$Record.FinalAppraisalValue}</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Appraisal Retro Add Trade-In To Quote {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Appraisal Retro Add Trade-In To Quote</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_TradeIn_Deduction_Line</name>
        <label>Create Trade-In Deduction Line</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>674</locationY>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_CustomerFacing__c</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_LineItemType__c</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Trade-In Deduction</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_RelatedTradeIn__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>PricebookEntryId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_TradeIn_PricebookEntry.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Product2Id</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_TradeIn_Product.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Quantity</field>
            <value>
                <numberValue>1.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>QuoteId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Existing_Quote.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>UnitPrice</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Formula_NegativeTradeInValue</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>QuoteLineItem</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Existing_Deduction_Line</name>
        <label>Get Existing Deduction Line For This Appraisal</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Line_Already_Exists</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>QuoteId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Existing_Quote.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>AF_RelatedTradeIn__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>QuoteLineItem</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Existing_Quote</name>
        <label>Get Existing Quote On Opportunity</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Has_Quote</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>OpportunityId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.ReferenceRecordId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Quote</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_TradeIn_PricebookEntry</name>
        <label>Get Trade-In Deduction Pricebook Entry</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>566</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Create_TradeIn_Deduction_Line</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Product2Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_TradeIn_Product.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Pricebook2Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Existing_Quote.Pricebook2Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>IsActive</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>PricebookEntry</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_TradeIn_Product</name>
        <label>Get Trade-In Deduction Product</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>458</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_TradeIn_PricebookEntry</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>ProductCode</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>AF-TRADEIN-DEDUCT</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Product2</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Existing_Quote</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>ISCHANGED({!$Record.AF_TradeInOutcome__c}) &amp;&amp; ISPICKVAL({!$Record.AF_TradeInOutcome__c}, &quot;Accepted&quot;) &amp;&amp; ISPICKVAL({!$Record.AF_ApprovalStatus__c}, &quot;Approved&quot;)</filterFormula>
        <object>Appraisal</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Update</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
